---
// Story 1-6, relaid out for story 1-16 (visual parity).
//
// ⚠️ THE CI TRIPWIRE IS GONE ON PURPOSE. The old placeholder carried a
// MLW-SPIKE-1 marker that the deploy workflow asserted. That assertion was
// removed in the SAME commit as this page, which is what the 1-2 comment warned
// had to happen. The per-commit proof is dist/build-id.txt, which lives outside
// page content and is unaffected.
//
// COPY DIRECTION IS MANNY'S, AND DECISION 3 IS LOCKED (MN-48, confirmed by
// Keegan 2026-07-31): the h1 carries the SERVICE and the brand tagline sits
// above it as styled text. "Move Better, Live Longer" is a good brand line that
// tells a search engine, and a stranger, nothing about what Keegan does.
//
// Sections are ANSWER-FIRST (MN-48 decision 1): every h2 is a question a real
// person asks, and the first 40-60 words answer it outright before any context.
//
// ─── 1-16: WHAT CHANGED HERE, AND WHAT DELIBERATELY DID NOT ───────────────
// Keegan preferred the site he built himself: "most of that is probably in the
// pictures, the formatting, the visuals." So the LAYOUT is now measured off the
// live target at keegansmovementlab.com — full-bleed photographic hero, one very
// large display heading, a dark green field behind the middle of the page, white
// cards with a photo on top, pill buttons.
//
// THE WORDS ARE UNCHANGED and the decided content still stands: chiro-primary,
// mobility coaching folded in, MPA at $160, the launch nav. He asked for the
// LOOK back, not the outdated information. The palette does not revert either —
// the old site's #ff3502 was his own hand-approximation and he chose the real
// brand palette on 08-01. Layout from the old site, colour and type from the
// brand.
//
// The four cards mirror the target's four-card grid and reuse THE SAME
// PHOTOGRAPHS it uses for them, but the services are ours, not its: mobility
// coaching is folded into chiropractic, so the second card is the Movement Plan
// Analysis rather than a retired standalone service.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BookCta from '../components/BookCta.astro';
import business from '../data/business.json' with { type: 'json' };

import Carousel from '../components/Carousel.astro';

import heroSquat from '../assets/site/IMG_1496-scaled.jpg';

// ─── CAROUSEL IMAGES, AND WHY THESE ONES ──────────────────────────────────
// The target runs two carousels here, one after the service cards and one near
// the foot. These are drawn from the 27 images 1-15's editorial pass left
// deliberately unplaced — a gallery is the one context where "more pictures of
// the work" is the point rather than padding.
//
// ⚠️ THE SELECTION IS CONSTRAINED BY AN OPEN QUESTION, ON PURPOSE. UD-29 (Argus,
// 2026-08-02) asks whether the people whose faces show clearly on this site
// agreed to be on it, and whether the woman on the home page is actually a
// patient. That is unanswered. Adding twenty more identifiable faces would
// multiply an unresolved consent question on a health business's front page, so
// every image below is either Keegan himself or a treatment shot where the
// patient is not identifiable (face down, or only a limb in frame).
// There are better clinical photographs available and they are NOT used yet.
// Revisit once UD-29 is answered.
import mov1 from '../assets/site/IMG_1528.jpg';
import mov2 from '../assets/site/IMG_1537-scaled.jpg';
import mov3 from '../assets/site/IMG_1542.jpg';
import mov4 from '../assets/site/IMG_1550-scaled.jpg';
import mov5 from '../assets/site/IMG_1570-scaled.jpg';
import mov6 from '../assets/site/IMG_1604.jpg';
import mov7 from '../assets/site/IMG_1607.jpg';
import mov8 from '../assets/site/2-man-pike-scaled.jpg';

import clin1 from '../assets/site/prone-tx.jpg';
import clin2 from '../assets/site/prone-palpation-3-scaled.jpg';
import clin3 from '../assets/site/glute-massage-scaled.jpg';
import clin4 from '../assets/site/Feet-test.jpg';
import clin5 from '../assets/site/Supine-knee-test-2-scaled.jpg';
import clin6 from '../assets/site/Keegan-Photos-32.jpg';

// Alt text written after looking at each photograph at real size, not from the
// filename — alt written from a thumbnail is confidently wrong alt, and alt is
// a public accessibility surface (MLW-LRN-29).
const MOVEMENT = [
  { src: mov1, alt: 'Keegan in a seated straddle fold, chest lowered to the floor between his legs' },
  { src: mov2, alt: 'Keegan in a deep low lunge, back knee down and chest upright, in a mirrored studio' },
  { src: mov3, alt: 'Keegan lying on his back in a supine spinal twist, one knee crossed over the body' },
  { src: mov4, alt: 'Keegan in a straddle handstand, legs split wide above him' },
  { src: mov5, alt: 'Keegan in a tucked handstand, knees drawn in over his shoulders' },
  { src: mov6, alt: 'Keegan in a standing forward fold, legs straight and hands flat on the floor' },
  { src: mov7, alt: 'Keegan folding forward over straight legs, head close to his shins' },
  { src: mov8, alt: 'Two people side by side in a seated pike fold, reaching along their legs' },
];

const CLINIC = [
  { src: clin1, alt: 'Keegan treating a patient lying face down on a treatment table, hands on the mid-back' },
  { src: clin2, alt: 'Keegan palpating along the spine of a patient lying face down' },
  { src: clin3, alt: 'Keegan applying hands-on soft-tissue work to a patient’s hip, patient lying face down' },
  { src: clin4, alt: 'Close view of Keegan holding and testing the movement of a patient’s foot and ankle' },
  { src: clin5, alt: 'Keegan testing the range of a patient’s bent knee, only the leg in frame' },
  { src: clin6, alt: 'Keegan supporting a patient’s lower leg while assessing how the joint moves' },
];
// The four card photographs, matched to the ones the live site uses for its own
// four-card grid so the page reads as the same page.
import cardChiro from '../assets/site/Keegan-Photos-36.jpg';
import cardMobility from '../assets/site/Seated-Shoulder-Rom-2-scaled.jpg';
import cardClasses from '../assets/site/Keegan-demonstrating.jpeg';
import cardHandstand from '../assets/site/IMG_1551.jpg';
import splitAdjust from '../assets/site/Rib-adjust.jpg';

const LAST_CHANGED = new Date('2026-08-02T00:00:00+10:00');
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Movement-Focused Chiropractor, Northern Beaches | ${business.name}`}
  description="Movement-focused chiropractic in Wheeler Heights on Sydney's Northern Beaches. Get out of pain, find out why it happened, and build a body that keeps up. 30-minute appointments with Keegan Baldwin."
  updated={LAST_CHANGED}
>
  {/* ── HERO ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      The photograph is blurred and dimmed into a ground rather than shown as
      a picture, which is what the target does (its hero asset is literally
      named blur-pike-1.png). That is not only a style choice: orange display
      text over a BRIGHT photograph measures between 1.02 and 2.05:1, and this
      is a white-curtain studio. Against the dimmed ground it is 3.85:1, which
      clears the 3.0 large-text bar. Do not lighten the scrim without
      re-measuring the painted pixels behind the words. */}
  <section class="hero">
    <Image
      src={heroSquat}
      alt=""
      aria-hidden="true"
      widths={[768, 1280, 1920]}
      sizes="100vw"
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
    {/* 🔴 THE h1 CARRIES THE SERVICE. DO NOT PUT THE BRAND LINE BACK IN IT.
        MN-48 decision 3, confirmed by Keegan 2026-07-31: "service-led h1,
        tagline as styled brand text. Not open; build to it."

        This exact shape is Manny's locked draft, reproduced:
            (styled brand line, small, above)  Keegans Movement Lab · Live Better, Longer
            # Movement-focused chiropractic on the Northern Beaches
            (sub) Get out of pain, find why it happened, and build a body that keeps up.

        I BROKE THIS MYSELF in the 1-16 parity work and Foundry caught it
        (LN-13, via Manny's FD-22 P2.1). Copying the old site's look brought its
        brand-line h1 back with it, against a carve-out that story carried in
        bold. Worth naming: parity was the thing the work was MEASURED on and
        the decision was only written down, so parity won. A carve-out in a
        story is not a control.

        Why it is more than tidiness: the h1 is the strongest on-page statement
        of what the business does, and "Move better, live longer" tells a search
        engine nothing. It is the same entity-confusion that got Keegan's Google
        Business Profile edits rejected — on the page that matters most. */}
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <p class="kicker">{business.name} · Live Better, Longer</p>
      <h1>Movement-focused chiropractic on the Northern Beaches</h1>
      <p class="lead">Get out of pain, find why it happened, and build a body that keeps up.</p>
      <BookCta slug="new-patient" label="Book an appointment" />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── THE FIELD ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      The target runs one continuous dark-green-into-sage field behind the
      middle of the page rather than alternating bands, with a centred intro
      and the card grid sitting on it. */}
  <section class="section section--wide section--field section--fade">
    <div class="intro">
      <p class="kicker">Movement health services</p>
      <h2>What is movement-focused chiropractic?</h2>
      <p>
        It is chiropractic that treats how you move, not just where it hurts. I settle the acute
        problem, find the movement pattern behind it, and give you a plan so it stops coming back.
        Appointments are 30 minutes rather than 10, which is what makes that possible.
      </p>
      <BookCta slug="new-patient" label="Book an appointment here" />
    </div>

    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <Image
          src={cardChiro}
          alt="Keegan standing behind a seated patient with her arms folded across her chest, his arms wrapped around her shoulders to set up a seated upper-back adjustment"
          widths={[400, 800]}
          sizes="(max-width: 40rem) 100vw, 35vw"
        />
        <div class="card-body">
          <h3>Chiropractic consultation &amp; treatment</h3>
          <p>
            If you have pain or stiffness, start here. Spinal and joint adjustments, hands-on muscle
            release and massage, and rehab based on what your assessment actually showed rather than
            a generic sheet. $120 for the first hour, $95 for a 30-minute follow-up.
          </p>
          <p><a href="/services/chiropractic-treatment/">More about chiropractic and movement</a></p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <Image
          src={cardMobility}
          alt="Keegan testing a seated patient's shoulder range of motion, guiding the arm overhead while steadying the shoulder blade"
          widths={[400, 800]}
          sizes="(max-width: 40rem) 100vw, 35vw"
        />
        <div class="card-body">
          <h3>Movement Plan Analysis</h3>
          <p>
            If you want more out of your body rather than relief from pain, this is the one. A full
            mobility assessment that finds the weak links holding your range back, and a
            personalised routine to address them. $160 for one hour.
          </p>
          <p><a href="/services/">Full services and pricing</a></p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <Image
          src={cardClasses}
          alt="A group class in progress in a gym studio, participants working through a movement drill on mats while Keegan demonstrates"
          widths={[400, 800]}
          sizes="(max-width: 40rem) 100vw, 35vw"
        />
        <div class="card-body">
          <h3>Weekly group classes</h3>
          <p>
            The lowest-commitment way in. Mobility and flexibility on Wednesdays, both open to
            complete beginners, at Just Train Gym in Cromer. $20 for an hour.
          </p>
          <p><a href="/services/group-classes/">More about group classes</a></p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <Image
          src={cardHandstand}
          alt="Keegan holding a straight handstand in a mirrored studio, legs together and fully extended"
          widths={[400, 800]}
          sizes="(max-width: 40rem) 100vw, 35vw"
        />
        <div class="card-body">
          <h3>Handstand coaching and classes</h3>
          <p>
            Handbalancing from the first kick-up to a freestanding hold, coached with the same
            assessment-led approach. Saturday mornings, and worth checking the booking page for the
            week's session.
          </p>
          <p><a href="/services/handstand/">More about handstand coaching</a></p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── CAROUSEL 1 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      The target puts an image carousel directly after its service cards, on
      the same field. Same position here. No autoplay — see Carousel.astro. */}
  <section class="section section--wide section--sage">
    <div class="intro">
      <p class="kicker">What the work looks like</p>
      <h2>What does three months of mobility look like?</h2>
      <p>
        Range you can actually use, in positions you could not hold before. These are the shapes the
        training builds toward, and every one of them is trainable from wherever you start now.
      </p>
    </div>
    <Carousel label="Movement and mobility photographs" slides={MOVEMENT} />
    <div class="intro">
      <BookCta slug="movement-plan-analysis" label="Book a movement plan analysis" />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── SPLIT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      The target's second half is a two-column image-and-text block on the
      lighter end of the field. Same shape here, carrying the "who is this
      for?" answer. */}
  <section class="section section--wide section--sage">
    <div class="split">
      <Image
        src={splitAdjust}
        alt="Keegan performing a hands-on thoracic adjustment on a patient lying face down on a treatment table"
        widths={[480, 960]}
        sizes="(max-width: 40rem) 100vw, 45vw"
      />
      <div>
        <h2>Who is this for?</h2>
        <p>
          Anyone in pain or stiffness who wants to know why, and anyone with no pain at all who
          wants more out of their body. Those are the same problem seen at two stages. All ages,
          demographics and levels of health and fitness are welcome.
        </p>
        <p>
          If your shoulder, hip or knee is part of the problem, we address it. Most patients need
          fewer visits overall.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── CAROUSEL 2 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      The target's second carousel sits near the foot of the page. Same here,
      on ink so the two do not read as one repeated block. */}
  <section class="section section--wide section--field">
    <div class="intro">
      <p class="kicker">In the clinic</p>
      <h2>What does treatment actually involve?</h2>
      <p>
        Hands-on assessment and treatment, then something specific to do between visits. Thirty
        minutes is what makes that possible rather than a ten-minute adjust-and-go.
      </p>
    </div>
    <Carousel label="Photographs of treatment in the clinic" slides={CLINIC} />
    <div class="intro">
      <BookCta slug="new-patient" label="Book an appointment here" />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── THE PLAIN TAIL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      Back on the reading measure. The practical answers a visitor scrolls for
      do not want a decorative treatment. */}
  <h2>What does it cost?</h2>
  <p>
    An initial consultation is $120 for one hour. A follow-up is $95 for 30 minutes. A Movement Plan
    Analysis, which is the full mobility assessment and personalised routine, is $160 for one hour.
    Treatments are health fund rebatable if you have chiropractic cover as an extra, and you can
    claim at the time of payment or later with an invoice.{' '}
    <a href="/services/">Full services and pricing</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Where are you, and when are you open?</h2>
  <p>
    I practise from {business.address.venue} at {business.address.streetAddress},{' '}
    {business.address.addressLocality}, on Sydney’s Northern Beaches. Full opening hours, the address
    and my phone number are at the bottom of every page on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to next?</h2>
  <ul class="next-links">
    <li><a href="/contact/">Book an appointment</a></li>
    <li><a href="/services/chiropractic-treatment/">Chiropractic &amp; Movement</a> — the main service page</li>
    <li><a href="/about/">About Keegan</a> — background and approach</li>
    <li><a href="/services/">Services and pricing</a></li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .next-links {
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }
  .next-links li {
    margin: 0.35rem 0;
  }
</style>
